<title>RUSSIA: Russian crop sowing shrinks four pct, grains flat.</title>
<headline>Russian crop sowing shrinks four pct, grains flat.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crop sowing contracted four percent this year, but grain plantings were flat, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>Sugarbeet sowings declined 12 percent while sunflowerseed plantings dropped 10 percent.</p>
<p>The committee released the following preliminary assessment of the areas sown to crops for harvesting in 1997. The numbers include plantings by private farmers:</p>
<p>	 AREAS OF RUSSIAN CROPS SOWN FOR HARVESTING IN 1997</p>
<p>			     Area sown for	pct change</p>
<p>			     1997 harvest	 yr/yr</p>
<p>			     (million hectares)</p>
<p> Total sown area	  95.7 -4</p>
<p> grains (incl maize,    53.5		  -1</p>
<p>or corn)</p>
<p> sugarbeet  (1,000 ha)  944		  -12</p>
<p> sunflowerseed	     3.6		 -10</p>
<p> soybeans (1,000 ha)    389		  -20</p>
<p>Russia has forecast a flat grain harvest this year of a net 70 million tonnes, a notch above last year's 69.3 million tonnes, which was one of the poorest on record in three decades.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
